      "writtenOn": "2025-01-08T21:05:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "From GLSLang, I don\u0027t think so? From my reading of teh docs, I believ `gl_PerVertex` is special, it isn\u0027t really a struct in GLSL, as you access the members directly `gl_Position`, etc. So, gl_PerVertex is just, like, a holder? of things that get accessed in other ways.\n\n\u003e gl_PerVertex defines an interface block for outputs. The block is defined without an instance name, so that prefixing the names is not required.\n\u003e \n\u003e https://www.khronos.org/opengl/wiki/Built-in_Variable_(GLSL)",
      "parentUuid": "c57422e4_f2e92d28",
      "revId": "f1c28fe8671ffba7ea7b5411b6ed0615a140d9b2",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
