      "writtenOn": "2025-01-08T22:54:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I see that the old SPIR-V reader does not support this and asserts if it happens. We should probably do the same, otherwise users might be surprised (since this is not a SPIR-V restriction, some non-glslang tools might do it).\n\nAlso, the `PointSize` member *will* be accessed (to assign 1.0), so this isn\u0027t really the right logic anyway. We should instead just always skip both `CullDistance` and `PointSize`. We can assert that `CullDistance` is not accessed using `IsIndexAccessed()`, but I don\u0027t think we should make decisions using it.",
      "parentUuid": "3bbc3a5f_9131ffa7",
      "revId": "f1c28fe8671ffba7ea7b5411b6ed0615a140d9b2",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
